mdv: "1.0"
title: JSON data
---

# Tail latency by service

Records arrive shaped for a program rather than for a table, so `latency`
is an object and not two columns. Flattening gives it path names — and a
path is an ordinary field name once it has one, which is why `y:` can bind
`latency.p99` without knowing the value was ever nested.

Field order is the first record's key order. `region` is absent there and
appears only in the second, so it is appended rather than sorted into
place, and the record that never had it reads empty.

```mdv bar
title: p99 latency by service
x: service
y: latency.p99
format: json
---
[
  { "service": "gateway", "latency": { "p50": 12, "p99": 41 } },
  { "service": "search", "latency": { "p50": 18, "p99": 96 }, "region": "eu" }
]
```
